Analysis:
  - Vulnerability CWE-190 (integer overflow in r->x + r->w) requires
    r->x near INT_MAX. Standard PGS/DVB/DVDSUB/XSUB subtitle formats
    all use 16-bit coordinates (max 65535), which cannot produce
    the overflow condition.
  - The bounds check at ffmpeg_filter.c:319 correctly handles 16-bit
    out-of-bounds coordinates by logging and returning early.
  - To trigger the actual overflow, a subtitle decoder would need to
    produce r->x >= 536870912 (0x20000000) or r->y >= similar value.
